./DESIGN.md-29-  through J104 and are labelled as J1.1 brown +12 V, J1.2 white GND, J1.3 green
./DESIGN.md-30-  RS-485 A, and J1.4 yellow RS-485 B.
./DESIGN.md-31-- The 7–15 V input uses a resettable fuse, input TVS, reverse-polarity P-FET,
./DESIGN.md-32-  AP63205 fixed 5 V buck, and separate TPS7A2033 digital and analog 3.3 V rails.
./DESIGN.md-33-  The analog LDO input is isolated from `+5V` by fitted R32=10 ohm and bypassed
./DESIGN.md-34-  locally by C7=10 uF X7R plus C27=100 nF on `+5V_ANALOG`. R32 uses an 0805
./DESIGN.md-35-  option footprint that may take 0 ohm or a characterized bead after testing;
./DESIGN.md-36-  a bead is not the default because its low-frequency inductance can resonate
./DESIGN.md:37:  near the ADS1119 256 kHz modulator frequency.
./DESIGN.md:38:- The O2 signal chain is SGX three-electrode cell -> LMP91000 -> ADS1119. U15,
./DESIGN.md-39-  an **AZ431B wired as a two-terminal 2.5 V shunt** (REF strapped to the
./DESIGN.md:40:  cathode), establishes `VREF_SHUNT`, and R31 feeds `VREF_TRIM` from it; that
./DESIGN.md-41-  net keeps its name only because firmware keys off it, and **there is no
./DESIGN.md-42-  trimmer**. `POTTING.md` §1.2 (in `../../../ha/farming/compostlab/o2-probe/`)
./DESIGN.md-43-  removed it: the cell must be swappable with the board potted, so no adjustable
./DESIGN.md-44-  part may sit on the potted side.
./DESIGN.md-45-  - R41 biases the shunt from `+5V_ANALOG`, **not** 3V3A. The part needs
./DESIGN.md-46-    I_KA ≥ 1.0 mA, and 3V3A leaves only 3.234 − 2.510 = 0.724 V of worst-case
./DESIGN.md-47-    headroom — about 6 % over that floor — where +5V_ANALOG leaves 2.5 V and
./DESIGN.md-48-    gives 1.67 mA.
--
./DESIGN.md-68-  the bias telemetry through R38, so the guard tracks the **real** electrode
./DESIGN.md-69-  instead of the old open-loop 0.91×VREF replica, which is both strictly better
./DESIGN.md-70-  guarding and the ADC channel that makes the bias measurable. `GUARD_REPLICA`
./DESIGN.md-71-  keeps its name because `repair_guard_fill.py`, `route_thermal_barrier.py` and
./DESIGN.md-72-  `audit_pcb.py` key off it; it is no longer a replica of anything.
./DESIGN.md-73-  No femtoampere part is needed: RE already carries the LMP91000's own ±900 pA
./DESIGN.md-74-  max IRE (SNAS518, −40..80 °C), so the OPA333's ±200 pA max at 25 °C raises the
./DESIGN.md-75-  worst case by about 20 %, where an ADA4530-1 at 20 fA would leave it at 900 pA.
./DESIGN.md:76:- ADS1119 AIN2/AIN3 read `WE_BUF`/`RE_BUF` **differentially** as the cell bias.
./DESIGN.md-77-  SBAS925 allows the ~2.27 V common mode at gain 1 and 4 alike, giving ±625 mV
./DESIGN.md-78-  full scale at gain 4. The two rail monitors this displaced, `VA_MON` and
./DESIGN.md-79-  `VIN_MON`, are now both on the MCU's own ADC (PA7/IN7 and PA6/IN6).
./DESIGN.md-80-- The processor is STM32G071CBT7. USART1 on PA9/PA10 drives the THVD1410 farm
./DESIGN.md-81-  RS-485 port. USART2 on PA2/PA3 is reserved for the expansion/recovery path.
./DESIGN.md-82-- PC6 drives `RS485_DE`, placing the direction-control GPIO beside the USART1
./DESIGN.md-83-  TX/RX pins, and PA7/ADC_IN7 measures `VA_MON`. These pin choices are
./DESIGN.md-84-  generator-owned because they make the compact right-side MCU placement
