./DRDY-FIX.patch-6-      * before trusting anything the part says. */
./DRDY-FIX.patch-7-+    /* DRDY is an input this driver polls, and until now NOTHING configured
./DRDY-FIX.patch-8-+     * it. PB1 comes out of reset in ANALOG mode (MODER = 11), which
./DRDY-FIX.patch-9-+     * disconnects the input buffer so IDR reads 0 forever - regardless of
./DRDY-FIX.patch-10-+     * R19 holding the real pin high. The wait in convert_once() therefore
./DRDY-FIX.patch-11-+     * fell through on its FIRST evaluation, RDATA was issued before the
./DRDY-FIX.patch-12-+     * conversion had finished, and the part returned the PREVIOUS
./DRDY-FIX.patch-13-+     * conversion. Every channel read as whichever channel preceded it, which
./DRDY-FIX.patch:14:+     * is exactly the "AIN3 mirrors AIN0" signature that got a healthy
./DRDY-FIX.patch:15:+     * ADS1119 replaced. It also disabled O2P_ADS_TIMEOUT, a guard that
./DRDY-FIX.patch-16-+     * cannot fire when the wait it protects never happens.
./DRDY-FIX.patch-17-+     * No internal pull: R19 pulls the line up on the board. */
./DRDY-FIX.patch-18-+    O2P_ADC_DRDY_PORT->MODER &= ~(3u << (O2P_ADC_DRDY_PIN * 2u));
./DRDY-FIX.patch-19-+
./DRDY-FIX.patch-20-     s_last_cfg = 0xFFu;   /* a reset invalidates any cached configuration */
./DRDY-FIX.patch-21-     const uint8_t rst = O2P_ADS_CMD_RESET;
