./o2-probe.xml-2445-        <field name="MPN">OPA2333AIDGKR</field>
./o2-probe.xml:2446:        <field name="Design Note">Both halves are now unity-gain electrometer followers on the cell nodes: A buffers WE, B buffers RE and drives both the guard (through R40) and the ADC bias telemetry. Half A was freed by deleting the VREF trim divider. NO FEMTOAMPERE PART IS NEEDED HERE and this is the reason: SBOS351E gives OPA333 IB as +/-70 pA typ and +/-200 pA max at 25 C. MIND THE ARITHMETIC: IB is the AVERAGE of the two inputs, and a follower's electrode sees the non-inverting input alone, so the real bound is |IB| + |IOS|/2 = 200 + 200 = 400 pA. The RE node is ALREADY loaded by the LMP91000's own RE pin at +/-90 pA typ and +/-900 pA max over -40..80 C (SNAS506I IRE, TI's own front-page feature; at this board's 3.3 V the applicable column is nearer 800 pA). So half B takes RE's worst case from ~900 pA to ~1300 pA, +44%, and an ADA4530-1 at 20 fA would still leave ~900 pA and buy nothing. UNSTATED ASSUMPTION, flagged deliberately: SBOS351E gives NO max for IB over temperature, only +/-150 pA typ, so the claim that a chopper's charge-injection-dominated bias stays flat to 75 C rests on Figure 8, a typical curve, not a guaranteed limit. See POTTING.md section 1.3 under ../../../ha/farming/compostlab/o2-probe/</field>
./o2-probe.xml-2447-        <field name="Footprint">Package_SO:VSSOP-8_3x3mm_P0.65mm</field>
./o2-probe.xml-2448-        <field name="Datasheet"/>
./o2-probe.xml-2449-        <field name="Description"/>
./o2-probe.xml-2450-      </fields>
./o2-probe.xml-2451-      <libsource lib="o2-probe" part="OPA2333" description="Dual zero-drift rail-to-rail op amp"/>
./o2-probe.xml-2452-      <property name="MPN" value="OPA2333AIDGKR"/>
