./o2-probe.xml:2775:        <field name="Design Note">2.5 V reference, wired as a two-terminal shunt (REF strapped to the cathode). REPLACES the deleted R20 / RV1 / R21 trim divider: POTTING.md section 1.2 (../../../ha/farming/compostlab/o2-probe/) requires the cell to be swappable with the board potted, so no adjustable part may set the bias. AZ431-A datasheet Rev 3.4: B grade is the 0.4% bin, 2.490/2.500/2.510 V, and deviation over -40..85 C is 4.5 mV typ / 10 mV max, so the worst-case window is 2.480..2.520 V. PACKAGE PIN MAP IS NOT THE TI ONE -- N package is 1 REF, 2 CATHODE, 3 ANODE, where TI's TL431DBZ is 1 K, 2 REF, 3 A; see the symbol comment. Biased from +5V_ANALOG through R41 and NOT from 3V3A: the part needs IKA &gt;= 1.0 mA (recommended operating conditions) and 3V3A leaves only 3.234 - 2.510 = 0.724 V of headroom, about 6% margin over that minimum, where +5V_ANALOG leaves 2.5 V</field>
