./README.md:102:schematic. Those have already moved once — the input-voltage divider went from
./README.md-103-130k/20k to 82k/10k — and nothing but a comment connected the two.
./README.md-104-
./README.md-105-So `firmware/tools/gen_hw_contract.py` imports `gen_sch.py`, extracts every
./README.md-106-value the firmware converts with, and writes `firmware/src/hw_contract.h`. A
./README.md-107-PlatformIO pre-build action regenerates and diffs it, and `board_pins.h`
./README.md-108-static-asserts each GPIO binding against the generated pin map. A schematic
./README.md:109:change that rescales a divider or moves a pin now **breaks the build** instead
./README.md-110-of silently rescaling every reported value.
./README.md-111-
./README.md-112-```sh
./README.md-113-cd firmware
./README.md-114-python3 tools/gen_hw_contract.py          # regenerate after a schematic change
./README.md-115-python3 tools/gen_hw_contract.py --check  # what the build runs
./README.md-116-python3 tools/check_regmap_docs.py        # prose register map vs regmap.h
./README.md-117-```
