firmware/FIRMWARE.md-155-bytes at DR0 and 242 at DR5 — the 242 assuming no repeater and empty `FOpts`,
firmware/FIRMWARE.md-156-222 otherwise — but no data rate lets one downlink carry more than 40 bytes of
firmware/FIRMWARE.md-157-CFGDEV. Airtime is likewise not the limit: 785 SF12 downlinks of 57 PHY bytes
firmware/FIRMWARE.md-158-is 2,630 ms each, 2,064 s of transmitter time (0.57 h), which under continuous
firmware/FIRMWARE.md-159-10 % duty-cycle pacing on the 869.4–869.65 MHz band is about 5.7 h elapsed —
