./firmware/FIRMWARE.md-1242-- **Every reset costs 15 minutes of settling.** An earlier version skipped the
./firmware/FIRMWARE.md-1243-  wait when the reset was not a power-cycle and the LMP91000's registers read
./firmware/FIRMWARE.md-1244-  back intact. That inference does not hold: the readback proves the AFE's
./firmware/FIRMWARE.md:1245:  *digital* configuration survived, not that `VREF_TRIM` stayed present. An EMI
./firmware/FIRMWARE.md-1246-  event that resets the MCU can equally collapse the reference buffer for a few
./firmware/FIRMWARE.md-1247-  milliseconds, with VREF back long before the readback runs. Fifteen minutes
./firmware/FIRMWARE.md-1248-  of honest invalidity, at most once per reset, beats an unknown interval of
./firmware/FIRMWARE.md-1249-  confident wrong numbers from a buried instrument.
