./firmware/src/main.c-1-/* o2-probe Rev A - v0 application.
./firmware/src/main.c-2- *
./firmware/src/main.c-3- * A 1 Hz sample cycle feeding a Modbus RTU slave. No sleep modes: the probe is
./firmware/src/main.c-4- * PSU powered through the farm cable and the cell bias must run continuously,
./firmware/src/main.c-5- * so there is no power budget to optimise and every low-power mode is a way to
./firmware/src/main.c-6- * accidentally interrupt the bias.
./firmware/src/main.c-7- *
./firmware/src/main.c-8- * THE SAMPLER IS INCREMENTAL, one conversion per main-loop pass, and that is
./firmware/src/main.c:9: * not a stylistic choice. A full cycle is twelve ADS1119 conversions; at the
./firmware/src/main.c-10- * 20 SPS setting the oxygen channel alone wants eight of them at 50 ms each.
./firmware/src/main.c-11- * Run as one blocking routine that is ~500 ms during which nothing answers the
./firmware/src/main.c-12- * bus - half the master's likely timeout, spent ignoring it. Interleaved, the
./firmware/src/main.c-13- * worst case a Modbus reply can wait behind is a single conversion.
./firmware/src/main.c-14- *
./firmware/src/main.c-15- * What v0 deliberately does NOT do: drive the membrane heater (see heater.h).
./firmware/src/main.c-16- *
./firmware/src/main.c-17- * The RS-485 firmware updater (SCHEMATIC-REVIEW.md M2) IS here: update.c holds
--
