./firmware/src/main.c-608-     * inference does not hold: the readback proves only that the AFE's
./firmware/src/main.c:609:     * DIGITAL configuration survived, not that VREF_TRIM stayed present. An
./firmware/src/main.c-610-     * EMI event that resets the MCU can equally collapse the reference buffer
./firmware/src/main.c-611-     * for a few milliseconds; VREF recovers long before the readback happens,
./firmware/src/main.c-612-     * and the probe then publishes oxygen from a cell that genuinely needs
./firmware/src/main.c-613-     * another quarter of an hour.
./firmware/src/main.c-614-     *
./firmware/src/main.c-615-     * So: every reset settles. Fifteen minutes of honest invalidity, at most
./firmware/src/main.c-616-     * once per reset, beats an unknown interval of confident wrong numbers
./firmware/src/main.c-617-     * from a buried instrument.
