./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-263-- Reserve escape channels during placement. Opposite-side passives around U7
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-264-  boxed the fine-pitch 3V3A pad. Moving R33/C28 and escaping the pad along its
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-265-  axis before the via made the route solvable.
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-266-- Passive orientation is routing data. C9 initially faced its GND pad toward
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-267-  R21's wiper pad; rotating it 180 degrees turned an impossible crossing into
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-268-  a short direct bottom-layer connection.
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-269-- Limit rip-up authority to named blockers. The successful closure fixed
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-270-  `/3V3A` and `/VREF_WIPER`, then withdrew only `/I2C_SCL`, `/I2C_SDA`,
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md:271:  `/VIN_MON`, `/AFE_VOUT`, and `/ADC_VREF_MON`. KRT rerouted those five nets
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-272-  while every unrelated completed net remained protected.
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-273-- Reject router regressions with an improvement gate. KRT's reconciliation and
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-274-  multi-point phase can reopen previously connected nets; preserve accepted
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-275-  checkpoints and compare gained/lost connectivity before promotion.
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-276-- Route signal escapes before repairing planes. Router-created GND fragments
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-277-  were stripped, signals were closed, then `repair_planes.py` rebuilt GND taps.
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-278-- Plane repair's in-memory oracle can be newer than its first saved output.
./PCB-EXPERIENCE.md-279-  Reopen the written board, refill zones, and save again before DRC; otherwise
--
