248-+# AIN2/AIN3 are the bias-telemetry pair, read DIFFERENTIALLY as V_WE - V_RE.
249-+# POTTING.md section 1.1: VREF is NOT where the LMP91000's +/-2% bias step error
250-+# lives, so measuring VREF cannot substitute -- the differential is the only node
251-+# carrying the real information. SBAS925 permits this directly: absolute input
252-+# range is AGND-0.1 to AVDD+0.1 at gain 1 AND gain 4, so the ~2.27 V common mode
253-+# is unconstrained. BUT MIND THE PEDESTAL: with REFCN = 0xCD the internal zero is
254-+# 67% VREF and the bias step 24%, so V_WE = 1.675 V, V_RE = 2.275 V and their
255-+# DIFFERENCE IS -600 mV BY DESIGN -- 96% of the +/-625 mV full scale at gain 4,
256-+# not a small signal near zero. It does not clip only because the LMP91000 ladder
257:+# and the ADS1119 FSR are both referred to this same VREF_TRIM node, making the
258-+# ratio exact and VREF-independent. Two consequences: firmware must NOT convert
259-+# this channel against the ADS1119 internal 2.048 V reference the way
260-+# finish_vref() does for AIN1 (FSR becomes +/-512 mV and -600 mV hard-clips), and
261-+# gain 1 is the safer setting -- 76 uV/LSB is still far finer than the quantity
262-+# measured, with 2.5 V of headroom. The two rail monitors this displaces move to
263-+# the MCU's own ADC, which already carried VA_MON.
