1181-7.3.1.6.2 2-Lead Galvanic Cell In Ground Referred Configuration
1182-When the LMP91000 is interfaced to a galvanic cell (for instance to an Oxygen gas sensor) referred to the
1183-ground of the system, an external resistor needs to be placed in parallel to the gas sensor; the negative
1184-electrode of the gas sensor is connected to the ground of the system and the positive electrode to the Vref pin of
1185-the LMP91000, the working pin of the LMP91000 is connected to the ground.
1186-The LMP91000 is then configured in 2-lead galvanic cell mode and the Vref bypass feature needs to be enabled.
1187-In this configuration the Control Amplifier (A1) is turned off, and the output of the gas sensor is amplified by the
1188-Transimpedance Amplifier (TIA) which is configured as a simple non-inverting amplifier.
1189-The gain of this non inverting amplifier is set according the following formula:
1190-      Gain= 1+(RTIA/RLoad)                                                                                                                           (6)
